# O'Pip SHADOW feasibility-evidence capture (R4-B2 Slice 3A)
# Dedicated, bounded, non-overlapping evidence producer that converts committed
# FeatureSnapshots (the 60-second grid) into genuine feasibility.evidence.recorded
# records for the non-authoritative target spine. This is NOT the protected unified
# cycle: it runs as its own process on the one scheduler (cron) and never takes the
# unified-cycle lock, so it cannot delay or skip a protection cycle.
#
# Cadence: every minute, aligned to the F3 60-second evaluation grid. Capture is
# authorized only when OPIP_FEATURE_BUS_MODE=shadow AND
# OPIP_CANONICAL_WRITER_MODE=shadow; otherwise it is an explicit recorded no-op that
# opens nothing (no canonical store, no Kraken).
#
# Non-overlap is guaranteed INSIDE the container: the producer holds a process-level
# advisory lock (OPIP_FEASIBILITY_CAPTURE_LOCK) for the whole pass, so at most one
# capture process executes inside the container at any instant even if the host
# Docker client dies independently. The host flock is a cheap first-line guard only.
#
# Bounds (derived, not arbitrary; the whole pass must finish inside its minute):
#   * the producer reads one bounded batch of committed snapshots after its persisted
#     cursor, materializes the whole batch, then persists the advanced cursor, so
#     successive passes progress instead of re-reading the oldest batch.
#   * per-snapshot market reads use the SAME pass-bounded per-attempt timeout as the
#     Feature Bus producer (see capture_request_timeout_seconds), so one stalled
#     public request cannot consume the whole pass budget and leave no disposition.
#   * internal wall-clock budget: OPIP_FEASIBILITY_CAPTURE_BUDGET_SECONDS (default 45,
#     capped at 50) bounds how many batches one pass attempts.
#   * enforceable termination: in-container `timeout ... 50` with kill-after 5s, so
#     the Python process is dead by ~55s < the 60s slot. NO host-side timeout wraps
#     the docker exec call (that would release the only host lock while the
#     in-container process could continue).
#   * protection (the 60s unified cycle) is a separate process and is never contended.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

* * * * * root flock -n /var/run/opip-feasibility-capture.lock -c 'cd /opt/OHM-Trade-Agent-v1/OHM-Trade-Agent-v1 && /usr/bin/docker compose exec -T ohm-trade-agent timeout --signal=TERM --kill-after=5s 50 python -m app.jobs.capture_feasibility_evidence_shadow >> /var/log/opip-feasibility-capture.log 2>&1'
